G0907.def:
**βαπτίζω**
(βάπτω), [in LXX: [[2Ki.5.14|4Ki.5:14]] (טבל), [[Isa.21.4|Isa.21:4]], [[Jdt.12.7|Jdth.12:7]], Sir.31 (34)30 * ;]
**to dip, immerse, sink**;
1. generally (in Polyb., iii, 72, of soldiers **wading breast-deep**; in i, 51, of the **sinking** of ships); metaphorically, **to overwhelm** (Is, l.with; cf. MM, _Exp._, x); with cogn. accusative, βάπτισμα β., [[Mrk.10.38, 39|Mrk.10:38, 39]] [[Luk.12.50|Luk.12:50]]. Mid.,
2. **to perform ablutions, wash oneself, bathe** (Ki, Jth, Si, ll. with): [[Mrk.7.4|Mrk.7:4]] aor. pass, in same sense, [[Luk.11.38|Luk.11:38]]
3 Of ablution, immersion, as a religious rite, **to baptize**;
(a) (a) absol.; [[Mrk.1.4|Mrk.1:4]], [[Jhn.1.25, 26, 28; 3.22, 23, 26; 4.2; 10.40|Jhn.1:25, 26 28 3:22, 23, 26 4:2 10:40]], [[1Co.1.17|1Co.1:17]]; ὁ βαπτίζων (= ὁ βαπτιστής, M, _Pr._, 127), [[Mrk.6.14, 24|Mrk.6:14, 24]]; with accusative, [[Jhn.4.1|Jhn.4:1]], [[Act.8.38|Act.8:38]], [[1Co.1.14, 16|I Co.1.14, 16]]; with cogn. accusative, τὸ βάπτισμα, [[Act.19.4|Act.19:4]] (cf. [[Mrk.10.38|Mrk.10:38]], supr.); pass., **to be baptized, receive baptism**: [[Matt.3.13|Mat.3:13]], 14, 16, [[Mrk.16.16|Mrk.16:16]], [[Luk.3.7, 12, 21; 7.29|Luk.3:7, 12 21 7:29]] (τ. βάπτισμα) ib. 30, [[Act.2.41; 8.12, 13, 36; 9.18; 10.47; 16.15, 33; 18.8|Act.2:41 8:12, 13 36 9:18 10:47 16:15, 33 18:8]]; mid., 22:16 (M, _Pr.,_ 163);
(b) **with prepositions**: ἐν, of the element, [[Mat.3.6, 11|Mat.3:6, 11]] [[Mrk.1.4, 5, 8|Mrk.1:4, 5 8]], [[Luk.3.16|Luk.3:16]], [[Jhn.1.26, 31, 33; 3.23|Jhn.1:26, 31 33 3:23]], [[Act.1.5; 2.38; 10.48; 11.16|Act.1:5 2:38 10:48 11:16]], [[1Co.10.2|1Co.10:2]]; εἰς, of the element, purpose or result (Lft., _Notes_, 155), [[Mat.3.1; 28.19|Mat.3:1 28:19]], [[Mrk.1.9|Mrk.1:9]], [[Act.8.16; 19.3, 5|Act.8:16 19:3, 5]] [[Rom.6.3|Rom.6:3]], [[1Cor.1.13|1Co.1:13]] 15 10:2 12:13, [[Gal.3.27|Gal.3:27]]; with dative, ὕδατι, [[Luk.3.16|Luk.3:16]], [[Act.1.5; 11.16|Act.1:5 11:16]]; ὑπὲρ τῶν νεκρῶν, perh. to fulfil the wish of a dead friend, [[1Co.15.29|1Co.15:29]] (see _ICC_, in l.; cf. _DB_, i, 238ff.; _DCG_, i, 169a; ii, 605b; Cremer, 126).
† (AS)

G0908.def:
**βάπτισμα**, -τος, τό (βαπτίζω), prop., the result of the act, τὸ βαπτίζειν, as distinct from βαπτισμός, the act itself,
**immersion, baptism**;
1. metaphorically, of affliction: [[Mrk.10.38, 39|Mrk.10:38, 39]] [[Luk.12.50|Luk.12:50]].
2. **Of the religious rite of baptism**;
(a) **of John's baptism**: [[Mat.3.7; 21.25|Mat.3:7 21:25]], [[Mrk.11.30|Mrk.11:30]], [[Luk.7.29; 20.4|Luk.7:29 20:4]], [[Act.1.22; 10.37; 18.25; 19.3|Act.1:22 10:37 18:25 19:3]]; β. μετανοίας, [[Mrk.1.4|Mrk.1:4]], [[Luk.3.3|Luk.3:3]], [[Act.13.24; 19.4|Act.13:24 19:4]];
(b) **of Christian baptism**; [[Rom.6.4|Rom.6:4]], [[Eph.4.5|Eph.4:5]], [[Col.2.12|Col.2:12]] (Tr., -μῷ, which see), [[1Pe.3.21|1Pe.3:21]] (cf. Cremer, 130; Tr., _Syn._ §xcix).
† (AS)

G0991.def:
**βλέπω**,
[in LXX chiefly for ראה, also for פּנה, etc. ;]
1. **of bodily sight**;
(a) **to see, have sight** (opposite to τυφλὸς): [[Mat.12.22|Mat.12:22]], [[Jhn.9.7|Jhn.9:7]], [[Act.9.9|Act.9:9]], [[Rom.11.8|Rom.11:8]], [[Rev.3.18|Rev.3:18]], al.;
(b) **to perceive, look (at), see**: absol., [[Act.1.9|Act.1:9]] with accusative, [[Mat.7.3|Mat.7:3]], [[Mrk.5.31|Mrk.5:31]], [[Luk.6.41|Luk.6:41]], [[Jhn.1.29|Jhn.1:29]], al.; ὅραμα, [[Act.12.9|Act.12:9]] γυναῖκα, [[Mat.5.28|Mat.5:28]] βιβλίον, [[Rev.5.3|Rev.5:3]], 4; τ. βλεπόμενα, [[2Co.4.18|2Co.4:18]]
2. Metaphorical, of mental vision;
(a) **to see, perceive, discern**: absol., [[Mat.13.13|Mat.13:13]], [[Luk.8.10|Luk.8:10]]; δι ̓ ἐσόπτρου, [[1Co.13.12|1Co.13:12]] with accusative, [[Heb.2.9; 10.25|Heb.2:9 10:25]]; before ὅτι, [[Heb.3.19|Heb.3:19]], [[Jas.2.22|Jas.2:22]];
(b) **to consider, look to, take heed**: absol., [[Mrk.13.23, 33|Mrk.13:23, 33]]; with accusative, [[1Co.1.26|1Co.1:26]], al.; before πῶς, with indic., [[Luk.8.18|Luk.8:18]], [[1Co.3.10|1Co.3:10]], [[Eph.5.15|Eph.5:15]]; before τί, with indic., [[Mrk.4.24|Mrk.4:24]] before εἰς πρόσωπον, of partiality, [[Mat.22.16|Mat.22:16]], [[Mrk.12.14|Mrk.12:14]]. Colloq. (for ex. from π., V. Deiss., _LAE_, 122; M, _Pr._, 107; MM, _Exp._, x; Milligan, _NTD_, 50), β. ἑαυτόν: [[Mrk.13.9|Mrk.13:9]] before ἵνα μή, [[2Jn.8|II Jo 8]]; β. ἀπό, [[Mrk.8.15; 12.38|Mrk.8:15 12:38]]; before μή (cl. ὁρᾶν), with fut. indic., [[Col.2.8|Col.2:8]], [[Heb.3.12|Heb.3:12]]; id. with aor. subj., [[Mat.24.4|Mat.24:4]], [[Mrk.13.5|Mrk.13:5]].
3. Of situation and direction (Lat. specto), **to look, face** (towards), places, etc. (before πρός, Xen, _Hell._, vii, 1, 17; [[Ezk.40.23, 24|Eze.40:23, 24]]): before κατά, with accusative, [[Act.27.12|Act.27:12]] (cf. ἀνα-, ἀπο-, δια-, ἐμ-, ἐπι-, περ-, προ-βλέπω), see _DCG_, i, 446; ii, 596.
(AS)

G0945.def:
**βατταλογέω**, -ῶ (Rec. βαττολ-, D, βλαττ- = βατταρίζω, prob. onomatop.; see MM, see word; _DCG_, ii, 499b, 790a);
**to stammer, repeat idly**: [[Mat.6.7|Mat.6:7]] (Cremer, 765).†
(AS)

G0922.def:
**βάρος**, -εος, τό,
[in LXX: [[Jdg.18.21|Jdg.18:21]] (כּבד), [[Jdt.7.4|Jdth.7:4]], [[Sir.13.2|Sir.13:2]], [[2Ma.9.10|2Ma.9:10]], [[3Ma.5.47|3Ma.5:47]] * ;]
**weight**;
(a) **a weight, burden**, lit. and metaphorically: [[Mat.20.12|Mat.20:12]], [[Act.15.28|Act.15:28]], [[2Co.4.17|2Co.4:17]], [[Rev.2.24|Rev.2:24]]; ἀλλήλων τὰ β., **one another's faults**, [[Gal.6.2|Gal.6:2]] ἐν β., **burdensome**: [[1Th.2.6|1Th.2:6]], R, txt., but see infr.;
(b) in late Gk. (Soph., _Lex._, see word), **dignity, authority**: ἐν βάρει, [[1Th.2.6|1Th.2:6]] (R, mg.; see Milligan, _ICG_, in l.).†
_SYN._: ὄγκος, _an encumbrance_; φορτίον, **a burden**, that which is borne. (AS)

G0903.def:
**Βαλαάμ**, ὁ, indecl. (Heb. בִּלְעָם), as in LXX (FlJ has ὁ βάλαμος);
**Balaam** (Num.22-24): [[2Pe.2.15|2Pe.2:15]], [[Jude.11|Ju 11]], [[Rev.2.14|Rev.2:14]].†
(AS)
